<div class="nav_swiper" data-controller="nav-swiper" data-nav-swiper-target="root">
  <%# These are links that navigate — /live, /channels, another host entirely —
      and there is no tabpanel anywhere on the page. Dressing them as
      role="tablist" > role="group" > role="tab" produced three axe violations at
      once: the group broke the tablist's required children, the tabs lost their
      required tablist parent through it, and role="tablist" on <nav> overrode
      the navigation landmark, so everything inside stopped counting as landmark
      content. It is a navigation bar, so it says so; aria-current marks the
      active entry, which is the correct signal for a nav and was already here.
      Roving tabindex went with the tab roles: a tablist is one tab stop by
      design, but a nav should let Tab reach every link. %>
  <nav id="nav_sections" class="nav_swiper_bar" aria-label="Sections" data-brgen-shell-target="navSections">
    <% brgen_nav_groups.each do |group_label, items| %>
      <div class="nav_swiper_group" role="group" aria-label="<%= group_label.capitalize %>">
        <% items.each do |label, href| %>
          <% active = label.downcase == (active_vertical.to_s.presence || "front") %>
          <%= link_to label, href,
                class: "nav_link#{" active" if active}",
                "aria-current": ("page" if active) %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </nav>
  <%# Was an always-visible 46x5 grip pill at the top centre. It computed to
      46x44 with a pill radius, so it painted as a dim grey circle sitting over
      the nav — the most conspicuous thing on the page and the first thing
      anyone noticed. The pull-down gesture and pointer-at-the-top-edge reveal
      cover mouse and touch; this stays for keyboard and assistive tech, and
      shows itself only on focus, exactly like the skip link above it. %>
  <button type="button" class="nav_swiper_reveal" data-action="click->nav-swiper#toggle"
          aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="nav_sections" data-nav-swiper-target="grip">Show sections</button>
</div>
